      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Russell Township, home to Novelty, was organized April 2, 1827, the last of Geauga County's sixteen townships, named after pioneer Gideon Russell.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/novelty_ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Novelty sits within the Cleveland metro area, about 20 miles east of downtown, yet keeps a rural feel with wooded ridges and fields.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/novelty_ohio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area enjoys a humid continental climate, with cold, snowy winters and warm, humid summers averaging July highs of 81°F.",
